### frontend/src/components/admin
#### [MODIFY] [PanelAnalytics.tsx](file:///C:/Users/revin/Downloads/Capstone/frontend/src/components/admin/PanelAnalytics.tsx)
- Refactor `handleExecuteAction` and `handleDeclineAction` to utilize true optimistic updates.
- Store the previous `biData` state in a local constant before modifying `setBiData`.
- If the API execution fails (in the `catch` block), instantly restore the previous `biData` state *without* triggering a new network request to `/api/admin/intelligence/suggestions`. This dramatically improves UI resilience when the server is struggling.

---

### frontend/src/components/ui
#### [MODIFY] [Toast.tsx](file:///C:/Users/revin/Downloads/Capstone/frontend/src/components/ui/Toast.tsx)
- Refactor `showToast` to accept an optional `toastKey` string identifier as a third parameter.
- Replace the rigid string-matching deduplication (which checks for hardcoded text like `"telemetry"`) with key-based deduplication.
- If a toast is dispatched with a `toastKey` that matches a recently shown toast within a specific time window, suppress it.
- This creates a scalable pattern for developers to debounce/throttle any recurring toast notifications easily.

